cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "actari: a local research companion for the U.S. National Archives Catalog"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Ramm
abstract: >-
  actari is an open-source desktop tool for working with the U.S. National
  Archives (NARA) Catalog API. It performs metadata fetch, bulk download of
  digital objects, and assembly of one consolidated PDF per File Unit, with
  optional image recompression and OCR. A local FastAPI web UI offers
  search, job management, and a manifest-backed library view. Not affiliated
  with or endorsed by the U.S. National Archives and Records Administration.
keywords:
  - actari
  - NARA
  - national-archives
  - archives
  - genealogy
  - digital-humanities
  - historical-research
  - bulk-download
  - PDF-assembly
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rammc/actari"
url: "https://github.com/rammc/actari"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-21"
